  "query_preview": "(This evening through Wednesday)...\nIssued at 147 PM EST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Tonight...\n\nWidespread rain has exited the area to the east of central Indiana \nearly this afternoon. Radar showed additional patchy light rain \nacross portions of the forecast area as well as east central \nIllinois. Extensive cloud cover extended west beyond the Mississippi \nRiver, with a few breaks. \n\nWill keep some low PoPs around most areas through this afternoon \nbased on trends on radar. Temperatures will begin to fall across the \narea from west to east, with readings already falling across eastern \nIllinois as of 18Z. \n\nExpect the cloud cover to remain across the area tonight. Cannot \nrule out some patchy drizzle if enough forcing in the cloud layer \nremains, but for now am not confident enough of this happening to \ninclude in the forecast.\n\nCold advection will bring in cooler air, but cloud cover will help \nkeep readings from bottoming out. Will go a little above guidance \nfor lows given the cloud cover.\n\nThursday...\n\nSome warm advection and mixing will likely clear some of the clouds \nout of the forecast area for a while on Thursday, especially south. \nClouds will be on the increase though from the northwest during the \nafternoon ahead of the next system. If enough sunshine breaks out, \nhighs in the south will be in the lower and middle 60s. Elsewhere, \nhighs will be in the upper 50s to around 60.\n\nThursday night and Friday...\n\nAn upper trough and surface cold front will move through Thursday \nnight into Friday. There won't be much moisture to work with as the \nGulf will basically be cut off. Will go with some chance PoPs north \nThursday night closer to the better forcing and dry PoPs south. \n\nOn Friday, there may be some lake enhanced showers sneaking into the \nnortheast forecast area as colder air flows in, so will have some \nslight chance to chance PoPs for this.\n\nHighs on Friday will only be in the lower to middle 50s for most \nareas with the cold advection and partly to mostly cloudy skies.\n\nSaturday onward...\n\nCentral Indiana will generally remain in northwest flow aloft. This \nwill allow a couple of weak fronts to move through, but the Gulf \nwill but cut off keeping moisture out of the area. Will go with a \ndry forecast.\n\nThe fronts will not have much cooler air with them as they move \nthrough. This will allow temperatures to moderate from the lower and \nmiddle 50s on Saturday to the lower and middle 60s for most areas \nMonday through Wednesday.",
